{
 "dur": 73.0,
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.4,
   "chunks": [
    "How was the",
    "Brooklyn Bridge built?",
    "When it opened, it was the longest",
    "suspension bridge on Earth."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 6.65,
   "chunks": [
    "Work began in 1870.",
    "Its designer, John Roebling,",
    "had died,",
    "so his son Washington took over."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 13.74,
   "chunks": [
    "First, caissons:",
    "giant upside-down wooden boxes,",
    "sunk into the riverbed,",
    "where men dug",
    "in compressed air."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 20.8,
   "chunks": [
    "Brooklyn's sank 44 feet,",
    "Manhattan's 78.",
    "Workers got the bends,",
    "and Washington was left bedridden."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 28.18,
   "chunks": [
    "His wife Emily",
    "carried his orders.",
    "On the caissons, granite towers",
    "rose 276 feet."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 34.94,
   "chunks": [
    "On shore,",
    "anchorages:",
    "60,000 tons of stone,",
    "holding chains for the cables."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 40.56,
   "chunks": [
    "From 1877,",
    "wheels spun steel wire",
    "across the river.",
    "Four cables,",
    "19 strands each."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 47.75,
   "chunks": [
    "Then suspenders",
    "and diagonal stays",
    "hung the deck",
    "from the cables and towers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 52.82,
   "chunks": [
    "On May 24, 1883,",
    "it opened.",
    "Emily crossed first.",
    "About 150,000 people",
    "followed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 60.65,
   "chunks": [
    "Trains crossed",
    "until 1944.",
    "Since 2021,",
    "it even has",
    "a protected bike lane."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v11",
   "t": 67.45,
   "chunks": [
    "Congrats! You've discovered",
    "how the Brooklyn Bridge",
    "was built."
   ]
  }
 ]
}